{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Full Dev Pipeline",
  "description": "A manually triggered master pipeline that runs the full development workflow in sequence: 1) Pull GitHub issues to identify related work, 2) Analyze spec files for context, 3) Run code analysis (ruff for Python, ESLint for TypeScript), 4) Review code changes against project standards, 5) Run the test suite, 6) Create an issue-linked branch, commit, push, and open a PR. Trigger this hook when you're ready to finalize and ship your changes.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Execute the full development pipeline in order. Complete each step before moving to the next. Report progress after each step.\n\n**Step 1 — GitHub Issue Sync**\nUse the GitHub MCP tool (mcp_github_list_issues) to pull all open issues from the repository (owner: Piashsarker, repo: inec-election-results). List the open issues and identify which ones relate to recent code changes.\n\n**Step 2 — Spec Analysis**\nRead the spec files in .kiro/specs/ (requirements.md, design.md, tasks.md). Summarize what the current spec covers and verify that recent changes align with the spec's requirements and design decisions.\n\n**Step 3 — Code Analysis**\nRun linting and static analysis:\n- For Python files: run `cd backend && python -m ruff check . 2>&1` \n- For TypeScript files: run `cd frontend && npx next lint 2>&1`\nReport any issues found. If there are auto-fixable issues, fix them with `ruff check --fix .`\n\n**Step 4 — Code Review**\nReview all modified files (check `git diff` and `git diff --cached`). Verify:\n- Follows project architectural patterns (async-first backend, App Router frontend)\n- Includes proper type annotations\n- Uses project error handling patterns\n- No security issues (exposed secrets, SQL injection, unvalidated input)\n- Aligns with spec design decisions\nFix any issues found.\n\n**Step 5 — Run Tests**\nRun the test suite: `cd backend && python -m pytest tests/ --tb=short -q 2>&1`\nReport results. If tests fail, attempt to fix the issues and re-run.\n\n**Step 6 — Push and Create PR**\nIf all previous steps pass:\n1. Check `git status` for uncommitted changes\n2. Identify the most relevant GitHub issue number from Step 1\n3. Create branch: `issue/#<issue_number>` (or `issue/#0-<description>` if no issue applies)\n4. Stage changes (exclude .env and secrets): `git add .` then `git restore --staged '*.env*' '.kiro/settings/*'`\n5. Commit: `type(scope): description (#issue_number)`\n6. Push: `git push -u origin <branch>`\n7. Create PR via GitHub MCP tool targeting main, referencing the issue\n\nReport the final PR URL when complete."
  }
}